{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5371) to implement srd041-id requirements R3.1, R3.2, and R3.3 in the go-unix-utils project. This involves extending the existing `cmd/id` utility with:\n   - R3.1: `-n`/`--name` modifier flag that prints names instead of numeric IDs when combined with `-u`, `-g`, or `-G`. Using `-n` without a selection flag must produce an error.\n   - R3.2: `-r`/`--real` modifier flag that prints real UID/GID instead of effective when combined with `-u` or `-g`. Using `-r` without `-u` or `-g` must produce an error.\n   - R3.3: USER operand support — when a username is provided as an argument, query that user's identity instead of the current process. Nonexistent users must produce an error to stderr and exit 1.\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/id/main.go` and `cmd/id/id_test.go`. Must follow execution constitution, go style constitution, differential testing protocol, and SIGPIPE shared protocol.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing against GNU reference binary `gid` via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Go's `os/user` package for user/group lookup (`user.Lookup`, `user.LookupId`, `user.LookupGroupId`)\n   - `syscall.Getgroups()` for supplementary groups\n   - `os.Getuid()`, `os.Getgid()` for effective IDs; need real IDs via `syscall.Getuid()`, `syscall.Getgid()` for `-r` flag\n   - Flag parsing is hand-rolled (no cobra) with short flag bundling support (e.g., `-un`, `-gn`)\n   - 40-line function size limit (E8), 500-line file limit (E9), DRY enforcement (E10)\n   - No git commands allowed — orchestrator manages git externally\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd041-id.yaml`\n     - Full SRD for the id utility; defines R1-R4 requirement groups\n     - R3.1: `-n`/`--name` prints name instead of numeric ID when combined with selection flag; error without selection flag\n     - R3.2: `-r`/`--real` prints real UID/GID instead of effective; error without `-u` or `-g`\n     - R3.3: USER operand queries named user instead of current process; nonexistent user → stderr error + exit 1\n     - Non-goals: no SELinux `-Z`, no BSD `-p`, no NIS/LDAP beyond NSS\n\n   - `cmd/id/main.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Current implementation covers R1.1-R2.4\n     - `flags` struct has only `user`, `group`, `groups` bools — needs `name` and `real` added\n     - `parseFlags` returns `(remaining []string, flags)` — currently treats all remaining args as \"extra operand\" error; must change to accept USER operand\n     - `parseShortFlags` handles `u`, `g`, `G` — needs `n`, `r` added\n     - `printEffectiveUID()` prints `os.Getuid()` — needs name mode and real mode variants\n     - `printEffectiveGID()` prints `os.Getgid()` — needs name mode and real mode variants\n     - `printGroups()` prints numeric group IDs — needs name mode variant\n     - `printDefaultOutput()` uses `os.Getuid()`, `os.Getgid()`, `syscall.Getgroups()` — needs USER operand support\n     - Key existing code:\n     ```go\n     type flags struct {\n         user   bool\n         group  bool\n         groups bool\n     }\n     ```\n     ```go\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         args := os.Args[1:]\n         remaining, f := parseFlags(args)\n         checkConflictingFlags(f)\n         if len(remaining) > 0 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"id: extra operand '%s'\\n\", remaining[0])\n             // ... exits 1\n         }\n         // switch on f.user, f.group, f.groups, default\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/id/id_test.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Has `normBinaryName` normalizer replacing \"gid:\" with \"id:\" in error messages\n     - 10 existing test cases: default, -u, --user, -g, --group, -G, --groups, conflict_ug, conflict_u_G, conflict_g_G\n     - Needs new tests for: `-un`, `-gn`, `-Gn`, `--name` with each selection flag, `-ur`, `-gr`, `--real` with -u/-g, `-n` alone (error), `-r` alone (error), `-r -G` (error), USER operand (e.g., \"root\"), nonexistent user error\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only three files were read before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified the gap between existing implementation (R1-R2) and needed features (R3)\n   - Key design considerations identified:\n     - `flags` struct needs `name bool` and `real bool` fields\n     - `parseShortFlags` needs cases for `'n'` and `'r'`\n     - `parseFlags` needs `--name` and `--real` long flag handling\n     - Main function must allow remaining args as USER operand instead of erroring\n     - Need validation functions for `-n` without selection flag and `-r` without `-u`/`-g`\n     - For USER operand: use `user.Lookup(username)` to get uid/gid, then look up groups for that user\n     - For real IDs: use `syscall.Getuid()` and `syscall.Getgid()` instead of `os.Getuid()`/`os.Getgid()`\n     - All print functions need to accept parameters for which user to query and whether to print name/real\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extensive task description with role definition, repository context, project documentation (VISION, ARCHITECTURE, SPECIFICATIONS), SRD content, execution constitution, go style constitution, coding standards, task requirements for implementing srd041-id R3.1, R3.2, R3.3, acceptance criteria, design decisions, constraints, and package contracts.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — Instructed to provide analysis and summary only, no tool calls.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Extend `flags` struct with `name` and `real` boolean fields\n   - Add `-n`/`--name` and `-r`/`--real` to flag parsing (both short and long forms)\n   - Add validation: `-n` requires `-u`/`-g`/`-G`; `-r` requires `-u`/`-g`\n   - Change remaining args handling from error to USER operand support\n   - Implement user lookup by name (`user.Lookup`) for USER operand\n   - Implement group lookup for named users\n   - Modify print functions to support name output mode, real ID mode, and named user context\n   - Add differential test cases for: `-un`, `-gn`, `-Gn`, `-ur`, `-gr`, `-n` alone error, `-r` alone error, `-r -G` error, named user (e.g., \"root\"), nonexistent user error\n   - Run `go build -o bin/id ./cmd/id/`, `go vet ./cmd/id/`, and `go test ./cmd/id/ -count=1`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three required files (SRD, main.go, id_test.go) and was about to begin implementing the changes when the summary was requested. No code has been written or modified yet. The next step would be to write the complete modified `cmd/id/main.go` and `cmd/id/id_test.go` files.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the modified `cmd/id/main.go` with R3.1, R3.2, R3.3 support:\n   - Add `name` and `real` fields to the `flags` struct\n   - Add `-n`/`--name` and `-r`/`--real` to `parseFlags` and `parseShortFlags`\n   - Add validation for modifier flags requiring selection flags\n   - Change remaining args from error to USER operand\n   - Implement user lookup by name and group resolution for named users\n   - Modify all print functions to accept user context, name mode, and real mode\n   Then update `cmd/id/id_test.go` with new differential test cases covering all R3.x scenarios.\n   Then verify with `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test`.\n\n   The task description states: \"Implement srd041-id requirement R3.1 -- read the SRD for the full requirement text and acceptance criteria\", \"Implement srd041-id requirement R3.2\", \"Implement srd041-id requirement R3.3\", with acceptance criteria requiring the code to compile, pass vet, and pass differential tests.\n\nIf you need